From 73fa56dd40831bd3c4a6b893b73e83abfdfa248e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Hines <luke@hines.im>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 21:00:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vt: pass TerminalOptions by pointer to fix i386 C ABI bug

Zig's callconv(.c) on i386 misreads struct-by-value parameters from
the wrong stack offset. This causes ghostty_terminal_new to receive
corrupted cols/rows/max_scrollback values, resulting in either a
silent failure (no scrollback) or GHOSTTY_INVALID_VALUE (black screen).

The fix changes ghostty_terminal_new to accept const Options* instead
of Options by value. A new_ptr() wrapper handles the dereference,
keeping new() by-value for Zig test compatibility.

Can be reverted once Ghostty upgrades to Zig >= 0.16.0.

See: https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/24812
See: https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/1481
See: https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/25452
