+# Ghostty Patches
+
+Local patches applied to the Ghostty submodule (`ghostty/`). The submodule tracks these on the `ghosteel-patches` branch.
+
+To update the submodule to upstream and rebase patches:
+
+```bash
+cd ghostty
+git fetch origin
+git rebase origin/main
+```
+
+---
+
+## `vt: pass TerminalOptions by pointer to fix i386 C ABI bug`
+
+**Files:** `include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h`, `src/terminal/c/terminal.zig`, `src/terminal/c/main.zig`
+
+Zig's `callconv(.c)` on i386 misreads `extern struct` parameters passed by value — the callee reads fields from the wrong stack offset. This caused `ghostty_terminal_new` to receive corrupted `cols`, `rows`, and `max_scrollback` values, resulting in either zero scrollback history or `GHOSTTY_INVALID_VALUE` (black screen).
+
+The fix changes `ghostty_terminal_new` to accept `const GhosttyTerminalOptions*` (pointer) instead of `GhosttyTerminalOptions` (value). A `new_ptr()` wrapper in Zig handles the dereference; the internal `new()` keeps its by-value signature so the 70+ Zig unit tests remain unchanged.
+
+**Can be removed once Ghostty upgrades to Zig >= 0.16.0**, where the i386 C ABI bug is fixed.
+
+**References:**
+- https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/24812 (open, arch-x86)
+- https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/1481 (umbrella tracking issue)
+- https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/25452 (fixed in 0.16.0)
+
+**Note:** The `ghostty/example/` files are intentionally left unmodified — they're upstream reference code, not compiled by Ghosteel.
diff --git a/include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h b/include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h
index 9b573c36a..b862c08f1 100644
--- a/include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h
+++ b/include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h
@@ -958,14 +958,22 @@ typedef enum GHOSTTY_ENUM_TYPED {
  *
  * @param allocator Pointer to allocator, or NULL to use the default allocator
  * @param terminal Pointer to store the created terminal handle
- * @param options Terminal initialization options
+ * @param options Pointer to terminal initialization options
  * @return GHOSTTY_SUCCESS on success, or an error code on failure
  *
+ * @note Options are passed by pointer to work around a Zig C ABI bug on
+ * i386 where struct-by-value parameters are read from the wrong stack
+ * offset. This can be reverted to pass-by-value once Ghostty upgrades
+ * to Zig >= 0.16.0.
+ * @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/24812
+ * @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/1481
+ * @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/25452 (fixed in 0.16.0)
+ *
  * @ingroup terminal
  */
 GHOSTTY_API GhosttyResult ghostty_terminal_new(const GhosttyAllocator* allocator,
                                    GhosttyTerminal* terminal,
-                                   GhosttyTerminalOptions options);
+                                   const GhosttyTerminalOptions* options);
 
 /**
  * Free a terminal instance.
diff --git a/src/terminal/c/main.zig b/src/terminal/c/main.zig
index 648bdbe51..156f4958a 100644
--- a/src/terminal/c/main.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/c/main.zig
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ pub const style_is_default = style.style_is_default;
 pub const sys_log_stderr = sys.logStderr;
 pub const sys_set = sys.set;
 
-pub const terminal_new = terminal.new;
+pub const terminal_new = terminal.new_ptr;
 pub const terminal_free = terminal.free;
 pub const terminal_reset = terminal.reset;
 pub const terminal_resize = terminal.resize;
diff --git a/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig b/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
index ab719eb4a..0a73839a0 100644
--- a/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
@@ -228,6 +228,24 @@ const NewError = error{
     OutOfMemory,
 };
 
+/// C ABI entry point. Accepts options by pointer to work around
+/// struct-by-value ABI bugs on i386 in Zig < 0.16.0.
+/// @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/24812
+/// @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/1481
+/// @see https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/25452
+/// Can be removed once the minimum Zig version is >= 0.16.0.
+pub fn new_ptr(
+    alloc_: ?*const CAllocator,
+    result: *Terminal,
+    opts: *const Options,
+) callconv(lib.calling_conv) Result {
+    return new(alloc_, result, opts.*);
+}
+
+/// Zig-to-Zig entry point used by tests. Accepts options by value.
+/// Must retain callconv(lib.calling_conv) even though it's only called
+/// from Zig — new_ptr() calls through .c convention, so both sides
+/// must agree on the ABI for struct parameters.
 pub fn new(
     alloc_: ?*const CAllocator,
     result: *Terminal,
